# Node adapter configuration (ADR-014 §Adapter B; docs/02-architecture/10-backend-architecture.md
# §node). Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored — see root .gitignore) and replace every value
# below with real secrets before running against real user data. `pnpm --filter api dev:node`
# loads `.env` automatically (src/adapters/node/config.env.ts).

# --- Secrets (`Config` port — ADR-012 §Auth exact values) -------------------------------------
# Server-side pepper mixed into every stored password verifier hash: SHA-256(pepper || verifier).
# Generate a real value with, e.g., `node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"`.
SESSION_PEPPER=test-only-session-pepper-not-a-real-secret

# HMAC key used to derive a stable fake salt for unknown usernames on GET /api/auth/salt (no
# existence oracle). Generate the same way as SESSION_PEPPER, with a DIFFERENT random value.
SALT_HMAC_KEY=test-only-salt-hmac-key-not-a-real-secret

# The origin this app is served from — checked against the WebSocket upgrade's `Origin` header
# (core/routes/characters.ts). Must match exactly (scheme + host + port), no trailing slash.
APP_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:8787

# --- Server (src/adapters/node/server.ts) ------------------------------------------------------
# Bind host/port for the HTTP + WebSocket server.
HK_HOST=127.0.0.1
HK_PORT=8787

# Directory SQLite files (accounts.sqlite, streams.sqlite) are created/opened under. Default when
# unset: ./data relative to apps/api's own package root. The Windows self-host recipe (ADR-014
# §Adapter B, Task 12) points this at %ProgramData%\Herokeep\data via the service's own env config
# — that is the service-install step's concern, not a different code path here.
# HK_DATA_DIR=./data

# Directory the built Angular app (`pnpm --filter web build`) is served from. Default when unset:
# ../web/dist relative to apps/api's own package root.
# HK_WEB_DIST_DIR=../web/dist
